 Scope decisions (defaults applied, flag if you want different)

 - Fund category/sub-category are optional FKs (nullable Category/SubCategory), not required — a fund can be general-purpose for the month or earmarked to one taxonomy
 branch. Project already carries its own category/subcategory; this is a separate, coarser dimension on the fund itself, matching the spec's "Fund Category / Fund Sub
 Category" as tracked attributes of the fund record.
 - month: stored as LocalDate, normalized to the 1st of the month in the service layer (so 2026-06-15 and 2026-06-01 both save as 2026-06-01) — avoids adding a custom
 YearMonth JPA converter for no real benefit.
 - fundType: plain String (spec doesn't enumerate values, so no enum — same treatment as Project.currentCondition).
 - allocatedAmount / remainingAmount: persisted columns, maintained transactionally by the service whenever an allocation is created or deleted (not derived on every
 read) — same pattern as Project.priorityRank, which is also an explicitly-maintained field rather than a computed one.
 - spentAmount: persisted, defaults to 0, NOT auto-updated yet — there's no work-order/payment domain to consume it from. It's a placeholder column for that future
 slice, per the region→fund→project→contractor→work-order/payment sequence.
 - History/audit trail: deferred. Spec section 11 ("who changed what, old value, new value") is a cross-cutting concern for the whole system, not specific to Fund —
 out of scope here, same reasoning as deferring Project's photo/document uploads.
 - Allocation is immutable: no PUT update on FundAllocation — to change an amount, delete and recreate (this keeps the fund balance math a simple add/subtract pair
 instead of a diff).
 - Deleting an allocation reverses the fund's balance (allocatedAmount -= amount, remainingAmount += amount) but does not revert the project's status — once a project
 is marked ALLOCATED that's treated as a durable milestone, not something to silently roll back.

 New entities (package com.himaloyit.buildnation.cdm.*, table prefix cons_)

 Fund — cons_fund:
 - id, month (LocalDate, day=1), fundType (String)
 - category (@ManyToOne, nullable FK), subCategory (@ManyToOne, nullable FK)
 - receivedAmount, allocatedAmount (default 0), spentAmount (default 0), remainingAmount (= receivedAmount initially) — all BigDecimal
 - createdAt, updatedAt

 FundAllocation — cons_fund_allocation:
 - id, fund (@ManyToOne FK, required), project (@ManyToOne FK, required), amount (BigDecimal)
 - createdAt, updatedAt

 New exception: util/exceptions/InsufficientFundBalanceException — thrown when an allocation amount exceeds fund.remainingAmount. Add a handler in
 GlobalResponseEntityException returning 400 Bad Request (mirrors the existing EntityNotFoundException → 404 handler).

 Pattern to follow (already established in this codebase)

 - Plain CRUD entity: Category/CategoryService/CategoryController (nullable-FK variant: same shape, just nullable = true on the @JoinColumns and null-safe lookups in
 the service)
 - FK-lookup + business-rule service method: ProjectService.createProject (validates FKs exist before building the entity) — FundAllocationService.createAllocation
 follows this same shape plus the balance check and the project-status side effect
 - Exception + handler pattern: EntityNotFoundException + GlobalResponseEntityException.handleEntityNotFoundException
 (constituency-development-management/src/main/java/com/himaloyit/buildnation/cdm/controllers/advice/GlobalResponseEntityException.java)
